PHASE 21 — Automated Cron Reminders and Scheduled Jobs

Goal:
Build scheduled reminders and cron-compatible jobs.

Jobs:
- Lesson reminder 24 hours before
- Lesson reminder 1 hour before
- Level check reminder if not completed
- Student form reminder if not completed
- Homework reminder
- Low credits reminder
- Weekly AI summary generation queue
- Streak/badge checks
- Referral qualification checks

Important:
- Jobs should be safe to run multiple times.
- Prevent duplicate reminders.
- Use sent log table.
- Timezone default: Asia/Dubai.

Pages:
- /owner/settings/cron
- /owner/jobs
- /owner/jobs/logs

API/cron endpoints:
- /api/cron/send-lesson-reminders
- /api/cron/send-homework-reminders
- /api/cron/check-badges
- /api/cron/weekly-summaries

Security:
- Cron endpoints must use secret token or server-only mechanism.
- Do not expose open cron endpoints publicly without protection.

Acceptance criteria:
- Reminder jobs run manually in development.
- Duplicate reminders are prevented.
- Job logs are visible.
- Owner sees setup instructions.

Manual test checklist:
- Create upcoming lesson.
- Run reminder job.
- Confirm notification/email log.
- Run again and confirm no duplicate.
- Check job logs.

Stop condition:
Stop here. Test this phase before continuing.
